## Data in the release

### ProofWriter (CC BY 4.0)

`data/test.jsonl` contains records that CRUX derived from ProofWriter (the open-world sets depth5, birds_electricity,
and pararules). CRUX changed the format of the records.
Tafjord, O., Dalvi Mishra, B., Clark, P. (2021). ProofWriter: Generating Implications, Proofs, and Abductive Statements
over Natural Language. Findings of ACL 2021. arXiv:2012.13048.
Source: https://allenai.org/data/proofwriter
License: CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

### RuleTaker (Apache-2.0)

The ProofWriter sets above can contain theories and questions that come from RuleTaker. The release keeps its license
notice.
Clark, P., Tafjord, O., Richardson, K. (2020). Transformers as Soft Reasoners over Language. IJCAI 2020.
arXiv:2002.05867.
Source: https://allenai.org/data/ruletaker (archived snapshot 2023-02-08), https://github.com/allenai/ruletaker
License: Apache License 2.0, https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

### BoardgameQA (CC BY)

`data/benchmarks/boardgameqa.jsonl` contains records that CRUX derived from BoardgameQA. CRUX changed the format of the records.
Kazemi, M., Yuan, Q., Bhatia, D., Kim, N., Xu, X., Imbrasaite, V., Ramachandran, D. (2023). BoardgameQA: A Dataset for
Natural Language Reasoning with Contradictory Information. NeurIPS 2023 (Datasets and Benchmarks). arXiv:2306.07934.
Source: https://storage.googleapis.com/gresearch/BoardgameQA/BoardgameQA.zip
License: CC BY. The paper does not state a version.

### DynaBench of the DynaGuard paper (MIT)

`data/benchmarks/dynabench.jsonl` contains the 543 test records of the `DynaBench` subset. CRUX changed the format of
the records.
Hoover, M., Baherwani, V., Jain, N., Saifullah, K., Vincent, J., Jain, C., Kazemi Rad, M., Bruss, C. B., Panda, A.,
Goldstein, T. (2025). DynaGuard: A Dynamic Guardian Model With User-Defined Policies. arXiv:2509.02563.
Source: https://huggingface.co/datasets/montehoover/DynaBench
License: MIT.
The dataset card gives no copyright line. The DynaGuard repository LICENSE (MIT, read 2026-10-22) has:
Copyright (c) 2025 Monte Hoover
This data is not the Facebook "Dynabench" platform.

### Super-NaturalInstructions (task IDs and hashes only)

The release contains no task instance of Super-NaturalInstructions.
`data/benchmarks/supernat_ids.jsonl` holds the record ID, the task ID, and a SHA-256 hash of each evaluation record.
`data/benchmarks/supernat_tasks.json` holds the category and the `Instance License` value of each task.
Wang, Y., Mishra, S., Alipoormolabashi, P., et al. (2022). Super-NaturalInstructions: Generalization via Declarative
Instructions on 1600+ NLP Tasks. EMNLP 2022. arXiv:2204.07705.
Source: https://github.com/allenai/natural-instructions
The repository data, except the task instances, has the Apache-2.0 license.
Each task instance set has the license of the original dataset.
To rebuild the records, run `python -m crux.data.supernat`, and compare the hashes.

### Synthetic data

`data/train.jsonl`, `data/dev_id.jsonl`, `data/validation.jsonl`, and the synthetic part of `data/test.jsonl` come from
the CRUX generator (Step 3). The license is Apache-2.0.
